# Coverage-guided fuzzer for the SSRF guard.
#
# atheris ships native libFuzzer binaries, so it exists only on Linux. That is
# why the Fuzz job cannot run on a Windows runner, and why the target carries a
# pure-Python driver for local use.
#
# 3.1.0 is the first release publishing a cp314 manylinux wheel, which this
# repo's Python floor (>=3.14) requires.
#
# Regenerate the hashed lock with:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 \
#     --output-file requirements/ci-atheris.txt requirements/ci-atheris.in
atheris==3.1.0